cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  Please cite this project and the upstream manuscript. This is a conditional
  research draft; include the repository commit used until a release is archived.
title: "A sharper exponent for integer multiplication"
authors:
  - family-names: Colkitt
    given-names: Douglas
  - family-names: Prosz
    given-names: Aurel
license: Apache-2.0
type: software
repository-code: "https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds"
url: "https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds"
abstract: >-
  Exact rational certificates, source patches, and research notes for conditional
  improvements to OpenAI's integer-multiplication manuscript. Direct nonadjacent
  axis routing, shared finite circuits, auxiliary role sharing, an early-stopping
  guard bound, and tighter Gaussian setup support kappa = 2^-59. Paureel's
  fixed-exponent parameter refinement gives kappa = 1.7523184e-18, with an exact
  scoped supremum and integrated rational certificate. An earlier
  parameter-only witness gives kappa = 5.8e-33, near a certified ceiling under
  the original cost accounting. The complete upstream algorithmic theorem is assumed.
keywords:
  - integer multiplication
  - computational complexity
  - exact arithmetic
  - parameter optimization
  - reproducible research
